{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>הנה נא ידעתי etc.</b> Rabbi Joseph Kara explains: הנה נא ידעתי — that they would kill me and take you, for כי אשה יפת מראה את refers to the verse after it: והיה כי יראו אותך etc., והרגו אותי — this implies that he feared they would kill him if he said she was his wife, because they would want to lie with her, and they are commanded concerning forbidden relations. And this is difficult, for they are likewise commanded concerning bloodshed, and if he knew that they were scrupulous about what they are commanded, then he should not have feared they would kill him. And one may answer that it would be preferable to them to kill him and commit the sin of bloodshed once rather than come upon her without killing, for the Egyptians would fear lest he cry out against them to the king."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:20.923979983Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}